{"title":"2023 USAMO Problems/Problem 1","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_3\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 3</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#See_also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_USAMO_Problems/Problem_1&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>In an acute triangle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/2/a/e2a559986ed5a0ffc5654bd367c29dfc92913c36.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"44\" height=\"14\" />, let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/d/1/5d1e4485dc90c450e8c76826516c1b2ccb8fce16.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$M$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"21\" height=\"14\" /> be the midpoint of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/3/3/e33fe7d65facd8868f58b6e94ddc7f153a5a3f9f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{BC}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"18\" />. Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/4/4b4cade9ca8a2c8311fafcf040bc5b15ca507f52.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> be the foot of the perpendicular from <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/3/c3355896da590fc491a10150a50416687626d7cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/7/3/e73bc78b745edf7fe1e55dbfc3d914190faf5015.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AM$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"35\" height=\"14\" />. Suppose that the circumcircle of triangle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/7/b/a7b510ddc7cf8a87b5cc0dd15adf8480cd2e6945.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABP$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"44\" height=\"14\" /> intersects line <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/5/6c52a41dcbd739f1d026c5d4f181438b75b76976.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"14\" /> at two distinct points <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/5/ff5fb3d775862e2123b007eb4373ff6cc1a34d4e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/8/6/9866e3a998d628ba0941eb4fea0666ac391d149a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$Q$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"16\" height=\"18\" />. Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/9/fc97ef67268cd4e91bacdf12b8901d7036c9a056.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$N$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" /> be the midpoint of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/4/0/0400d2a78f3adac267e7621c65d063b35fe53ab1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{AQ}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"28\" height=\"19\" />. Prove that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/d/0/bd096f6d987ad71625f4170c44fd9d738b79e322.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$NB=NC$\" width=\"86\" height=\"12\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_USAMO_Problems/Problem_1&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/a/4/6a47ca0fe7cb276abc022af6ac88ddae1a9d6894.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$X$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" /> be the foot from <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/3/3/e33fe7d65facd8868f58b6e94ddc7f153a5a3f9f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{BC}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"18\" />. By definition, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/f/2/bf29466cad8c387649e2b61972deace897519034.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle AXM = \\angle MPC = 90^{\\circ}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"200\" height=\"15\" />. Thus, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/4/8/7486957f7c88beb381234083718a31912e12e6a2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle AXM \\sim \\triangle CPM$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"156\" height=\"18\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/2/c/d2c883387cb1973296cb11b2054cf394fe832035.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle BMP \\sim \\triangle AMQ$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"155\" height=\"18\" />. \n</p><p>From this, we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/d/17d1d8d1bb09330a1a4321df85b09e0cdc8970fd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{MP}{MX} = \\frac{MC}{MA} = \\frac{MP}{MQ}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -17px\" width=\"166\" height=\"43\" />, as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/1/c/b1c3163535c4826342ba74ea4bff04cb6f2a8b41.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$MC=MB$\" width=\"92\" height=\"12\" />. Thus, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/d/1/5d1e4485dc90c450e8c76826516c1b2ccb8fce16.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$M$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"21\" height=\"14\" /> is also the midpoint of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/2/f/42fb543400533dbfcf7bccdee3b618bcdc49faf8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$XQ$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"30\" height=\"16\" />.\n</p><p>Now, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/e/8/2e825f8de5e76acd2ed41a450603decf0c7414f4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$NB = NC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"88\" height=\"14\" /> if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/9/fc97ef67268cd4e91bacdf12b8901d7036c9a056.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$N$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" /> lies on the perpendicular bisector of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/3/3/e33fe7d65facd8868f58b6e94ddc7f153a5a3f9f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{BC}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"18\" />. As <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/9/fc97ef67268cd4e91bacdf12b8901d7036c9a056.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$N$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" /> lies on the perpendicular bisector of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/5/1/551f3f0469063e13fe75288d121c617ba16f4c69.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{XQ}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"31\" height=\"19\" />, which is also the perpendicular bisector of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/3/3/e33fe7d65facd8868f58b6e94ddc7f153a5a3f9f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{BC}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"18\" /> (as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/d/1/5d1e4485dc90c450e8c76826516c1b2ccb8fce16.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$M$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"21\" height=\"14\" /> is also the midpoint of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/2/f/42fb543400533dbfcf7bccdee3b618bcdc49faf8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$XQ$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"30\" height=\"16\" />), we are done. \n~ Martin2001\n~ SomebodyST (minor edits)\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_USAMO_Problems/Problem_1&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We are going to use barycentric coordinates on <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c3a2d2224f7d163b46d702132425d47828bf538.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle ABC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"61\" height=\"18\" />. Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/c/1/5c12b28a637be3bb4c707e2a5e4bce47aabeed31.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A=(1,0,0)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"94\" height=\"18\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/0/1/c015abd5846b8538042d38f167ec4d3abb8b4bb2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B=(0,1,0)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"95\" height=\"18\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/6/0/0601dfe585e5f1db64ff77ab451365145c24c9b2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C=(0,0,1)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"94\" height=\"18\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/0/5/20520aed0f4d38d4ba63fdbf54491f0e4555b3c5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a=BC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"65\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/d/0/4d0945ed672d46e0b3ce68eab77d3c8c97785ca4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b=CA$\" width=\"60\" height=\"13\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/1/4/114ba3529432afc9366c7bf2c908575b7f8ed901.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c=AB$\" width=\"59\" height=\"13\" />. We have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/f/b/1fb5112505bce7988d9cc8b91da48b484ab06729.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$M=\\left(0,\\frac{1}{2},\\frac{1}{2}\\right)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"123\" height=\"45\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/6/a/d6a80903db44d5eb62bb383a6511a5833a3526d8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P=(x:1:1)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"113\" height=\"20\" /> so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/5/265432797fab2788235bc02940d95ca9d9b57d82.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overrightarrow{CP}=\\left(\\frac{x}{x+2},\\frac{1}{x+2},\\frac{1}{x+2}-1\\right)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"265\" height=\"45\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/5/0/e506695b7c7d73acd8a66004cee5cb4ba53e34a3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overrightarrow{AM}=\\left(-1,\\frac{1}{2},\\frac{1}{2}\\right)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"151\" height=\"45\" />. Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/b/5/3b5bc4e868718f71c6bab0f1489cea52ccb6aa0b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overleftrightarrow{CP}\\perp\\overleftrightarrow{AM}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"88\" height=\"21\" />, it follows that\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/7/7/8774a16099bf43614563e9f59b300ea161eb65e3.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\begin{align*} a^2\\left(\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot\\frac{1}{x+2}+\\frac{1}{2}\\left(\\frac{1}{x+2}-1\\right)\\right)+b^2\\left(\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot\\frac{x}{x+2}-\\left(\\frac{1}{x+2}-1\\right)\\right)\\\\ +c^2\\left(\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot\\frac{x}{x+2}-\\frac{1}{x+2}\\right)=0. \\end{align*}\" width=\"521\" height=\"92\" />\nSolving this gives\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/4/6/f46af55f622c06ea0c8f0b11db8e8844679eb110.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[ x=\\frac{2b^2-2c^2}{a^2-3b^2-c^2} \\]\" width=\"137\" height=\"39\" />\nso\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/1/3/b134fccca3069ac67bf46ab3c50eb22e82974883.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[ P=\\left(\\frac{b^2-c^2}{a^2-2b^2-2c^2},\\frac{a^2-3b^2-c^2}{2a^2-4b^2-4c^2},\\frac{a^2-3b^2-c^2}{2a^2-4b^2-4c^2}\\right). \\]\" width=\"448\" height=\"43\" />\nThe equation for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/8/0/38054f87ce27ca0068b0ed685d6809b70f85c17a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(ABP)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"55\" height=\"18\" /> is\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/a/4/0a431e6df8acb6e9f7331534548de50f87789bf9.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[ -a^2yz-b^2zx-c^2xy+ux+vy+wz=0. \\]\" width=\"329\" height=\"19\" />\nPlugging in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/5/ff5fb3d775862e2123b007eb4373ff6cc1a34d4e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> gives <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/8/0/980113411db28cef19af839a617cbfbc250a74dd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$u=v=0$\" width=\"77\" height=\"12\" />. Plugging in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/4/4b4cade9ca8a2c8311fafcf040bc5b15ca507f52.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> gives\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/c/5/5c51b92055f6630b6adee4b39574bdab97b62280.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\begin{align*} -a^2\\left(\\frac{a^2-3b^2-c^2}{2a^2-4b^2-4c^2}\\right)^2-b^2\\cdot\\frac{a^2-3b^2-c^2}{2a^2-4b^2-4c^2}\\cdot\\frac{b^2-c^2}{a^2-2b^2-2c^2}\\\\ -c^2\\cdot\\frac{b^2-c^2}{a^2-2b^2-2c^2}\\cdot\\frac{a^2-3b^2-c^2}{2a^2-4b^2-4c^2}+w\\cdot\\frac{a^2-3b^2-c^2}{2a^2-4b^2-4c^2}=0 \\end{align*}\" width=\"496\" height=\"92\" />\nso\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/a/c/cacc5ed4245e3142586554d67b96c9894eb26a51.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[ w=\\frac{2b^4-2c^4+a^4-3a^2b^2-a^2c^2}{2a^2-4b^2-4c^2}=\\frac{a^2}{2}-\\frac{b^2}{2}+\\frac{c^2}{2}. \\]\" width=\"401\" height=\"39\" />\nNow let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/b/d/9bd9f2dc5e7ef092528294ffa1db4f4cdc823892.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$Q=(0,t,1-t)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"124\" height=\"20\" /> where\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/0/5/40569ae868c107d288ca900bf4308a5ec3d06c4a.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\begin{align*} -a^2t(1-t)+w(1-t)&amp;=0\\\\ \\implies t&amp;=\\frac{w}{a^2} \\end{align*}\" width=\"220\" height=\"61\" />\nso <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/e/a/4ea5d87a2a8f672ac53be2e61345323fd917bd3b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$Q=\\left(0,\\frac{w}{a^2},1-\\frac{w}{a^2}\\right)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"160\" height=\"35\" />. It follows that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/2/2/9226706e7929581ce4f48af5e57b0d3de406b164.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$N=\\left(\\frac{1}{2},\\frac{w}{2a^2},1-\\frac{w}{2a^2}\\right)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"190\" height=\"45\" />. It suffices to prove that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/5/6/b5640aeb11cfa95574e7b2b1396db5e505663109.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overleftrightarrow{ON}\\perp\\overleftrightarrow{BC}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"86\" height=\"21\" />. Setting <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/e/e/6ee4e42bc5e7374f0b2b36b46cc2b7476dc93848.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overrightarrow{O}=0$\" width=\"51\" height=\"22\" />, we get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/f/8/5f875f10b1d091790d4916fef1fd7117a1de2d53.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overrightarrow{N}=\\left(\\frac{1}{2},\\frac{w}{2a^2},1-\\frac{w}{2a^2}\\right)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"191\" height=\"45\" />. Furthermore we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/0/6c08f67143f71779e30f39ef699ba4d2e5139a7c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overrightarrow{CB}=(0,1,-1)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"127\" height=\"25\" /> so it suffices to prove that\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/f/bcf00717d151a33ae8a9e8342be0b6e3830aa19e.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\begin{align*} a^2\\left(-\\frac{w}{2a^2}+\\frac{1}{2}-\\frac{u}{2a^2}\\right)+b^2\\left(-\\frac{1}{2}\\right)+c^2\\left(\\frac{1}{2}\\right)=0\\\\ \\implies w=\\frac{a^2}{2}-\\frac{b^2}{2}+\\frac{c^2}{2} \\end{align*}\" width=\"384\" height=\"88\" />\nwhich is valid. <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/6/c/b6cf65b1f2fbdf388e3daeff9b96b34d3399d777.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\square$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />\n</p><p>~KevinYang2.71\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_3\">Solution 3</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_USAMO_Problems/Problem_1&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 3\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/a/4/6a47ca0fe7cb276abc022af6ac88ddae1a9d6894.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$X$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" /> be the foot from <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/3/f/b3f6f7cd16a47f33bebcf3fc361eeb808b630504.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BC.$\" width=\"31\" height=\"12\" /> Note that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/b/d/dbda6e3c6f2b6c4cb0aaf9bb93f71f9b4840a932.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle AXC=\\angle APC,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"142\" height=\"18\" /> so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/8/2/782753174ef4adebb4e1f87b4c7f7d8622ffa713.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(AXPC)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"75\" height=\"20\" /> is cyclic. Furthermore, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/3/b/e3bb4eeb347e74e025fd175c22f1f7275af0555e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AP$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" /> is the radical axis of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/8/0/38054f87ce27ca0068b0ed685d6809b70f85c17a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(ABP)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"55\" height=\"18\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/2/c/12c39165520b0341768377efdf5d8b06081e1e2c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(AXPC),$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"80\" height=\"20\" /> so since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/d/1/5d1e4485dc90c450e8c76826516c1b2ccb8fce16.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$M$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"21\" height=\"14\" /> lies on <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/6/f/16f66250786df748f8273cd4c5ecae751ece84a7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AP,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"30\" height=\"16\" /> we must have that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/8/7/787008641b4e8e6a65e309dfa879032704faf16b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BM\\cdot MQ=CM\\cdot MX,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"195\" height=\"18\" /> so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/d/1/5d1e4485dc90c450e8c76826516c1b2ccb8fce16.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$M$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"21\" height=\"14\" /> is the midpoint of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/6/1/c61557fac7334f7485ce319232914c5525b9a351.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$QX.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"37\" height=\"18\" /> Therefore, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/a/3/7a331c55e70e3ea87921562feb2c5bb3548d6c7e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$MN\\parallel AX\\perp BC,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"145\" height=\"20\" /> so we are done. \n~krithikrokcs\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_also\">See also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_USAMO_Problems/Problem_1&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: See also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:40%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_USAMO\" title=\"2023 USAMO\">2023 USAMO</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_USAMO_Problems\" title=\"2023 USAMO Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/resources.php?c=182&amp;cid=27&amp;year=2023\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b>First Problem</b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_USAMO_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2023 USAMO Problems/Problem 2\">Problem 2</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_USAMO_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2023 USAMO Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_USAMO_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2023 USAMO Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_USAMO_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2023 USAMO Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_USAMO_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2023 USAMO Problems/Problem 5\">5</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=USAMO_Problems_and_Solutions\" title=\"USAMO Problems and Solutions\"> All USAMO Problems and Solutions</a></b>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<!-